<script>
  window.onload = function() {
    document.title = "Loading...";
    setTimeout(function() {
      document.getElementById('spinner').style.display = 'none';
      document.getElementById('result').style.display = 'block';
      document.title = "Dynamic title";
    }, 5000);
  };
</script>

<div class="practice-page">
  <a href="/dynamic_loading" class="back-link">← Back to Dynamic Loading</a>
  <h1 class="practice-title">Dynamic Loading — Example 7</h1>
  <div class="practice-banner"><ul>
    <li>The page title starts as "Loading..." and changes to "Dynamic title" after 5 seconds</li>
    <li>Assert <code>driver.getTitle()</code> equals "Loading..." immediately after load</li>
    <li>Use <code>WebDriverWait</code> to wait until the title changes, then assert the new value</li>
  </ul></div>

  <h4>Example 7: Dynamic page title after 5 seconds</h4>

  <div id="spinner" style="margin-top:1rem; color:#64748b;">
    Loading... <img src="/img/ajax-loader.gif">
  </div>

  <div id="result" style="display:none; margin-top:1rem;">
    <img src="/img/a-few-moments.jpg" style="max-width:100%; border-radius:8px;" alt="a few moments later">
    <p style="margin-top:0.8rem; color:#16a34a; font-weight:600;">Done! Page title is now "Dynamic title".</p>
  </div>
</div>
